":"FeaturedImageTile","isEntitled":false,"isUserAuthed":false,"pageType":"home","description":"A short-eared owl (Asio flammeus) flies over the salt marshes of British Columbia’s Fraser River Delta at dusk. These owls fly low and slow as they hunt, relying primarily on acute hearing to drop down on prey hidden under grass coves.","ctas":[{"text":"See more photos","url":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/photo-of-the-day"}],"img":{"crps":[{"nm":"raw","aspRto":1.4993557886986932,"url":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/f048f8a5-2a51-4a53-bb45-7133f5190f47/BOTY_Ivan_Sjogren.jpg"},{"nm":"16x9","aspRto":1.7777777777777777,"url":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/f048f8a5-2a51-4a53-bb45-7133f5190f47/BOTY_Ivan_Sjogren_16x9.jpg"},{"nm":"3x2","aspRto":1.5,"url":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/f048f8a5-2a51-4a53-bb45-7133f5190f47/BOTY_Ivan_Sjogren_3x2.jpg"},{"nm":"square","aspRto":1,"url":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/f048f8a5-2a51-4a53-bb45-7133f5190f47/BOTY_Ivan_Sjogren_square.jpg"},{"nm":"2x3","aspRto":0.6666666666666666,"url":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/f048f8a5-2a51-4a53-bb45-7133f5190f47/BOTY_Ivan_Sjogren_2x3.jpg"},{"nm":"3x4","aspRto":0.75,"url":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/f048f8a5-2a51-4a53-bb45-7133f5190f47/BOTY_Ivan_Sjogren_3x4.jpg"},{"nm":"4x3","aspRto":1.3333333333333333,"url":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/f048f8a5-2a51-4a53-bb45-7133f5190f47/BOTY_Ivan_Sjogren_4x3.jpg"},{"nm":"2x1","aspRto":2,"url":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/f048f8a5-2a51-4a53-bb45-7133f5190f47/BOTY_Ivan_Sjogren_2x1.jpg"}],"rt":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/f048f8a5-2a51-4a53-bb45-7133f5190f47/BOTY_Ivan_Sjogren.jpg","src":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/f048f8a5-2a51-4a53-bb45-7133f5190f47/BOTY_Ivan_Sjogren.jpg","dsc":"A short-eared owl (Asio flammeus) flies over the salt marshes of British Columbia’s Fraser River Delta at dusk. Photographer Ivan Sjögren spent the evening watching five owls hunt, witnessing aerial fights and displays in which the birds clapped their wings together. These owls fly low and slow as they hunt, relying primarily on acute hearing to drop down on prey hidden under grass coves. They primarily hunt small mammals like meadow voles and mice. and frequently get into aggressive aerial fights with other daytime over the same territory and prey. This photograph was a winning entry in the 2026 Bird Photographer of the Year competition.","ttl":"A Moment in Flight"},"abstract":"A short-eared owl (Asio flammeus) flies over the salt marshes of British Columbia’s Fraser River Delta at dusk. These owls fly low and slow as they hunt, relying primarily on acute hearing to drop down on prey hidden under grass coves.","theme":"dark","title":"A Moment in Flight","tags":[{"name":"PHOTO OF THE DAY","id":"_none","type":"custom"}],"abTest":{"testId":"nat_geo_landing_page_tests-479","variantId":"variant_a_control-1956","type":"textHighlightTest","variant":"variant_a","abTest":"nat_geo_landing_page_tests-479*variant_a_control-1956"}}]}],"orientation":"horizontal","theme":"dark","tint":"notint","cmsType":"EnhancedFrame","modulePosition":3,"leadType":"none"},{"mods":[{"id":"9efd5437-177a-4c9b-8909-b25c0483d9db","cmsType":"StackModule","align":"left","edgs":[{"id":"8cc514b5-7a3e-4530-b2ef-c71d02e6696e","cmsType":"EmailInlineTile","title":"FILL YOUR INBOX WITH AWE  ","backgroundImage":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/2e2421a3-f3cb-485f-b482-753cce8baaa0/MossForest.adapt.885.1.jpg","errorMessage":"Please enter a valid email address.","mrktngMeta":{"cpgnCd":"20260827_Homepage_EmailSignUp_B"},"campaignName":"Natgeo_LOB_FOB","placeholder":"Enter your email","subtitle":"Get reminders that the world is still full of astonishing things. Sign up for Nat Geo emails.","success":{"description":"<p>Watch your inbox over the next few days for photos, stories, and special offers from us.<p>","header":"Thanks for signing up!"},"submitButton":"Sign Up"}]}],"abVariant":"nl-674*variant_b-3598","modulePosition":4,"leadType":"none"},{"mods":[{"id":"db37c79e-7a35-4f06-9988-038c94898ca4","cmsType":"StackModule","align":"left","edgs":[