,"aspRto":0.6666666666666666,"url":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/c8af7c33-b48f-4932-8328-f61c5ae856fc/MF4189_260503_007367_2x3.jpg"},{"nm":"3x4","aspRto":0.75,"url":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/c8af7c33-b48f-4932-8328-f61c5ae856fc/MF4189_260503_007367_3x4.jpg"},{"nm":"4x3","aspRto":1.3333333333333333,"url":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/c8af7c33-b48f-4932-8328-f61c5ae856fc/MF4189_260503_007367_4x3.jpg"},{"nm":"2x1","aspRto":2,"url":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/c8af7c33-b48f-4932-8328-f61c5ae856fc/MF4189_260503_007367_2x1.jpg"}],"rt":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/c8af7c33-b48f-4932-8328-f61c5ae856fc/MF4189_260503_007367.jpg","src":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/c8af7c33-b48f-4932-8328-f61c5ae856fc/MF4189_260503_007367.jpg","dsc":"Fewer than 400 bearded vultures roam the skies above Lesotho and South Africa. Raptor conservationist has built a specialized breeding program to help save the imperiled bird.","ttl":"MF4189_260503_007367"},"abstract":"To bring one of the world’s largest vultures back from the brink, Shannon Hoffman is searching cliffs, collecting eggs, and raising chicks by hand.","title":"Can This Bone-Eating Bird Be Saved?","tags":[{"name":"Animals","id":"fa010584-7bbf-3e92-90f9-586bb27fce94","type":"sources","uri":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals"}],"abTest":{"testId":"nat_geo_landing_page_tests-479","variantId":"variant_a_control-1956","type":"textHighlightTest","variant":"variant_a","abTest":"nat_geo_landing_page_tests-479*variant_a_control-1956"}},{"id":"4f7ebcc5-95fd-4e47-8099-a9bf28e293c0","cmsType":"RegularStandardPrismTile","isPremium":false,"isEntitled":false,"isUserAuthed":false,"pageType":"home","description":"The continent is home to rivers that flow thousands of miles, deserts that unspool for millions more, and some of the world’s most ancient forests. But living there isn’t always easy. See how these six species have adapted to thrive in Africa’s harshest ecosystems.","ctas":[{"url":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals/graphics/six-species-survive-african-ecosystems","text":"natgeo.ctaText.explore","icon":"interactive"}],"img":{"crps":[{"nm":"raw","aspRto":1.5003663003663004,"url":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/60b1166e-8d69-4b75-a48e-0e778fff9d59/frog_still_2.jpg"},{"nm":"16x9","aspRto":1.7777777777777777,"url":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/60b1166e-8d69-4b75-a48e-0e778fff9d59/frog_still_2_16x9.jpg"},{"nm":"3x2","aspRto":1.5,"url":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/60b1166e-8d69-4b75-a48e-0e778fff9d59/frog_still_2_3x2.jpg"},{"nm":"square","aspRto":1,"url":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/60b1166e-8d69-4b75-a48e-0e778fff9d59/frog_still_2_square.jpg"},{"nm":"2x3","aspRto":0.6666666666666666,"url":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/60b1166e-8d69-4b75-a48e-0e778fff9d59/frog_still_2_2x3.jpg"},{"nm":"3x4","aspRto":0.75,"url":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/60b1166e-8d69-4b75-a48e-0e778fff9d59/frog_still_2_3x4.jpg"},{"nm":"4x3","aspRto":1.3333333333333333,"url":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/60b1166e-8d69-4b75-a48e-0e778fff9d59/frog_still_2_4x3.jpg"},{"nm":"2x1","aspRto":2,"url":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/60b1166e-8d69-4b75-a48e-0e778fff9d59/frog_still_2_2x1.jpg"}],"rt":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/60b1166e-8d69-4b75-a48e-0e778fff9d59/frog_still_2.jpg","src":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/60b1166e-8d69-4b75-a48e-0e778fff9d59/frog_still_2.jpg","dsc":"frog","ttl":"home africa interactive new thumb"},"abstract":"The continent is home to rivers that flow thousands of miles, deserts that unspool for millions more, and some of the world’s most ancient forests. But living there isn’t always easy. See how these six species have adapted to thrive in Africa’s harshest ecosystems.","title":"The Secrets to Survival in Africa","tags":[{"name":"Animals","type":"sources","uri":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/animals"}],"abTest":{"testId":"nat_geo_landing_page_tests-479","variantId":"variant_a_control-1956","type":"textHighlightTest","variant":"variant_a","abTest":"nat_geo_landing_page_tests-479*variant_a_control-1956"}}]}],"orientation":"horizontal","theme":"dark","tint":"low","cmsType":"EnhancedFrame","modulePosition":5,"leadType":"none"},{"gradient":true,"mods":[{"id":"0e79381f-65fc-4406-a221-b450fbe592de","cmsType":"TVPromoModule","items":[{"id":"fa667a26-5ad2-4397-9fb1-1be14f1eec68","cmsType":"RegularImmersivePrismTile","isEntitled":false,"isUserAuthed":false,"pageType":"home","description":"National Geographic Explorer Bertie Gregory explores the extraordinary lives of bees, which are among the planet’s most important animals. Over three years, special cameras opened a rare window into a single hive, revealing its hidden world. With more than 20,000 bee species pollinating one-third of the world’s food, this series uncovers their astonishing architecture and intelligence, unlocking their secrets.","ctas":[{"text":"Watch Now","url":"https://www.disneyplus.com/browse/entity-059dc4ee-f790-476d-82b3-e418c1f96780"}],"title":"Secrets of the Bees","abTest":{"testId":"nat_geo_landing_page_tests-479","variantId":"variant_a_control-1956","type":"textHighlightTest","variant":"variant_a","abTest":"nat_geo_landing_page_tests-479*variant_a_control-1956"},"disableGradient":true,"immersive":true}]},{"id":"d92aaca6-f194-4810-9730-bfdb7e40028c","cmsType":"CarouselModule","cta":{"text":"See Shows","url":"https://www.disneyplus.com/","target":"_self"},"edgs":[{"id":"2266be9a-150f-406f-abcb-6f7fbadd5d19","cmsType":"FeaturedContentTile","isEntitled":false,"isUserAuthed":false,"pageType":"home","ctas":[{"url":"https://www.disneyplus.com/browse/page-dd58eeed-9ecc-481d-8129-a8fa93601b5c","text":"natgeo.ctaText.seeMore","icon":"article"}],"img":{"crps":[{"nm":"raw","aspRto":0.75,"url":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/b90dd1b2-0781-47ca-99c6-d7b3753cff3d/Sharkfest_NG-Homepage_1920x2560.jpg"},{"nm":"16x9","aspRto":1.7777777777777777,"url":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/b90dd1b2-0781-47ca-99c6-d7b3753cff3d/Sharkfest_NG-Homepage_1920x2560_16x9.jpg"},{"nm":"3x2","aspRto":1.5,"url":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/b90dd1b2-0781-47ca-99c6-d7b3753cff3d/Sharkfest_NG-Homepage_1920x2560_